WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.373
Welcome to AI at Work. In the next minute, you will see

00:00:05.523 --> 00:00:10.896
how to use generative AI productively and responsibly in a professional environment.

00:00:11.046 --> 00:00:18.104
Generative AI can help draft text, suggest ideas, summarise material, or structure

00:00:18.254 --> 00:00:25.311
information. It predicts useful responses, but it does not guarantee factual accuracy.

00:00:25.461 --> 00:00:30.455
A good use case is preparing a first draft of a meeting agenda,

00:00:30.605 --> 00:00:35.598
a training outline, or a message using information you are allowed to share.

00:00:35.748 --> 00:00:41.619
Instead of saying write an email, explain the audience, purpose, tone,

00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:47.640
and required format. Clear instructions improve the usefulness of the draft.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:54.540
Do not enter confidential client information, personal records, or restricted documents

00:00:54.690 --> 00:01:01.440
into unapproved AI tools. Follow your organisation’s data and technology policies.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:08.262
A polished answer may still contain errors, invented references, or unsuitable advice. Check

00:01:08.412 --> 00:01:15.085
meaningful claims against reliable sources and keep human approval in the workflow.

00:01:15.235 --> 00:01:21.565
Use the model to support judgment, not replace it. Be especially

00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:28.044
careful with legal, financial, or other consequential decisions. Escalate uncertain cases.

00:01:28.194 --> 00:01:33.805
Now continue the course. Decide when to use AI, practise a

00:01:33.955 --> 00:01:39.565
stronger prompt, and apply responsible review to a realistic workplace scenario.
